<p>Israel said Friday that it carried out an airstrike in Gaza City targeting Izz al-Din al-Haddad, whom it identified as the head of Hamas’s armed wing in the Gaza Strip and one of the planners of the Hamas-led Oct. 7, 2023, attack on Israel. Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu and Defense Minister Israel Katz later said Israeli forces had killed al-Haddad; Hamas did not immediately comment on Israel’s claim. Gaza medical officials said Israeli strikes killed at least seven Palestinians, including a child, and wounded dozens; Al Jazeera reported that three women and a child were among civilians killed. Reports said one strike hit an apartment building in the Rimal neighborhood and another struck a nearby vehicle. Israel said al-Haddad had led Hamas’s military wing in Gaza after Mohammad Sinwar was killed last year and accused him of responsibility for killings, abductions and harm to Israeli civilians and soldiers. Hamas-led militants killed about 1,200 people in Israel and took 251 hostages in the Oct. 7, 2023, attack.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/RmQRIAu1WRMMbsRXLjpB3d7zkYdrkU0xYgmH0g-c3opxCleReBZXuGusTt7QAaepSQwxf4zh7ZLG79gYpbeDNrFkTeeLbJPLk-Rh7srhzES5Kg2ba3rRVw37MamPBqss9XBl1O6aoFGvOv4q4jYmrXiD2Ymj1MxclCmz0gdvNv2O6JGKb6fr2ykoxoQQK1DRU5RPf2d6LF7bnF5NgU2oYOf3G6e0siKpvuoVxpnnCkIakPnEZCaTr58qXWYaV0kvLkz1y8ychD8Y-agMLWZXwj-Ucgsc8qVnvK4SANG2Z5Qdki39xvvoHFSCuJ8zdiid_9asxlHhH73AuCOvT_xeIn2S_YEqNXQdDWDHvGH1F9b-BucmQXM' alt='Gaza residents look at a building hit in the Israeli strike targeting Izz al-Din al-Haddad.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Operational timing: A military spokesperson said Israel sent its air force to carry out the strike shortly after receiving information on al-Haddad’s whereabouts.</li><li>Ceasefire context: Reuters-based reporting carried by Nettavisen said the strike was the highest-ranking Hamas target hit since an October 2025 agreement intended to end major fighting.</li><li>Approval process: Annahar reported that Israeli Chief 